                <pb facs="0290" n="192" sameAs="frus:frus1900/pg192"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Conger to Mr. Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Pekin, China</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1900-09-04"><hi rendition="#italic">September 4,
                        1900</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Continuing my dispatch No. 400, of the 3d
                    instant, I have the honor to inclose translations of two proclamations which
                    were found prominently posted in the city, giving additional and conclusive
                    proof of the responsibility of the Chinese Government for the Boxer
                    movement.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">E. H. Conger.</hi></signed></closer>




